      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hi @surenb@google.com\n\nThis is a cherry pick from aosp/3081365, but I modify the interface to pass the whole vm_fault instead of just file and offset. I see more and more vendors adding hooks inside this path (just look at what we had in 6.1 kernel and there are 4 hooks inside this function). I want to rule them all and this is what I observed from other\u0027s need:\n\n1. To monitor data of interest from vm_fault, vmf-\u003evma, etc\n2. To enable/disable or tune the size of fault_around runtime\n\nHence I decide to pass vm_fault and pointer to fault_around and this should be enough to achieve all the above needs and hopefully we no longer need to have so many similar hooks here. Hope that make sense.",
